  "worked_solution": "We find the area of the region bounded by the graph of the curve and the $x$-axis by calculating the integral\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{9+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe break up the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{9+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{1}{9+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{9+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nEvaluating the first of these integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{1}{9+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}\\frac{1}{9+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}\\frac{3}{9+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061\\frac{x}{3}|}_{a}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\operatorname{arctan}\u20610-\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061\\frac{a}{3}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061\\frac{a}{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the integrand is an **even** function. This means that we can immediately deduce that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{9+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since both improper integrals exist, we conclude that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{9+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{1}{9+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{9+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
